.TH "libnvmf_exclusion_remove" 9 "libnvmf_exclusion_remove" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_exclusion_remove \- remove an entry by exact content match (atomic write).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_exclusion_remove
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "const char *name "  ","
.BI "const char *entry "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
libnvme global context; must not be NULL
.IP "name" 12
list name
.IP "entry" 12
entry string to remove, exactly as returned by
\fBlibnvmf_exclusion_entry_for_each\fP (e.g. "transport=tcp;traddr=192.168.1.1")
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, -ENOENT if the entry or list does not exist, negative errno otherwise.
